  "You've hit your session limit \u00b7 resets 4:20am (Asia/Singapore)",
  "## Design\n\n**Strategy.** The submarine parks at column 8 facing left (back cell at column 9) and only moves vertically after that. Fire is the default action, so its bullets sweep the whole row to its left.\n\n- **Positioning (row 0, which is safe):** move right until the sub touches column 9, then one step left to end at column 8 facing left, then dive.\n- **Hunting (rows 2\u20138):** move toward rows that hold an enemy in columns 0\u20134, nearest first. Stay and fire when one is in the current row. Idle at row 5.\n- **Dodging:** leave the row if anything dangerous is at columns 5\u20137 (an incoming bullet) or column 9 (an enemy spawning behind).\n- **Never enter** a row with danger at columns 5\u20139, and never move toward a row two away with danger at columns 7\u20139, because a sticky action can repeat the move.\n- **Divers:** a diver at columns 7\u20139 within three rows pulls the sub to that row, where it waits for the diver to step onto column 8.\n- **Oxygen:** when oxygen is below 60 the sub rises. Rows 2\u21921\u21920 are only crossed if the diver bar shows at least one diver; after refilling it dives again.\n\n**Hidden layer 1** (19 units used). Each unit is gated by the sub's row: the two player cells add +20000 against a \u221220000 bias, so only the unit for the current row is unsaturated and all others sit at exactly \u22121.\n\n| Units | Role |\n|---|---|\n| 0, 1, 2 | Row 0: move right, move left, dive |\n| 3 | Row 1: keep descending |\n| 4, 5 | Rows 1 and 2: go up only when surfacing (has diver and low oxygen) |\n| 6\u201311 | \"Go up\" score for rows 3\u20138 |\n| 12\u201317 | \"Go down\" score for rows 2\u20137 |\n| 18 | Row 2: weak emergency escape upward |\n\nThe up/down scores add these terms, from weakest to strongest: target pull \u00b1(2\u20267), hold on a target in my row \u221230, low oxygen \u00b1100, diver \u00b1250, threat in my row +1000, entry veto \u221220000.\n\n**Hidden layer 2.** Four units sum the up, down, right and left families and re-squash them. The outputs are 12 \u00d7 those, with fire at +2 and no-op at \u221220.\n\nNothing was run, so this is untested.\n\n```edits\n# ---------- row-0 positioning ----------\nW1[0:54:6, 0] = 10\nb1[0] = -15\nW1[54, 1] = 10\nW1[52, 1] = 10\nb1[1] = -15\nW1[54, 2] = 10\nW1[58, 2] = 10\nW1[91:120:6, 2] = -100\nW1[163:180:6, 2] = -100\nb1[2] = -15\n# ---------- unit 3: Down from row 1 ----------\nW1[108, 3] = 10000\nW1[114, 3] = 10000\nW1[557, 3] = 10\nW1[151:180:6, 3] = -20000\nW1[223:240:6, 3] = -20000\nb1[3] = -20005\n# ---------- unit 4: Up from row 1 (surface: diver & low oxygen) ----------\nW1[108, 4] = 10000\nW1[114, 4] = 10000\nW1[593, 4] = 10\nW1[557, 4] = -10\nb1[4] = -20005\n# ---------- unit 5: Up from row 2 (surfacing only) ----------\nW1[168, 5] = 10000\nW1[174, 5] = 10000\nW1[593, 5] = 10\nW1[557, 5] = -10\nW1[91:120:6, 5] = -20000\nb1[5] = -20005\n# ---------- unit 6: Up from row 3 ----------\nW1[1:600:60, 6] = [0, 0, 7, -30, -5.6, -4.8, -4, -3.2, -2.4, 0]\nW1[7:600:60, 6] = [0, 0, 7, -30, -5.6, -4.8, -4, -3.2, -2.4, 0]\nW1[13:600:60, 6] = [0, 0, 7, -30, -5.6, -4.8, -4, -3.2, -2.4, 0]\nW1[19:600:60, 6] = [0, 0, 7, -30, -5.6, -4.8, -4, -3.2, -2.4, 0]\nW1[25:600:60, 6] = [0, 0, 7, -30, -5.6, -4.8, -4, -3.2, -2.4, 0]\nW1[31:600:60, 6] = [0, 0, -20000, 1000, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0]\nW1[37:600:60, 6] = [0, 0, -20000, 1000, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0]\nW1[43:600:60, 6] = [0, -20000, -20000, 1000, 250, 250, 250, 0, 0, 0]\nW1[49:600:60, 6] = [0, -20000, -20000, 1000, 250, 250, 250, 0, 0, 0]\nW1[55:600:60, 6] = [0, -20000, -20000, 1000, 250, 250, 250, 0, 0, 0]\nW1[44:600:60, 6] = [0, 0, 250, -250, -250, -250, -250, 0, 0, 0]\nW1[50:600:60, 6] = [0, 0, 250, -250, -250, -250, -250, 0, 0, 0]\nW1[56:600:60, 6] = [0, 0, 250, -250, -250, -250, -250, 0, 0, 0]\nW1[228, 6] = 10000\nW1[234, 6] = 10000\nW1[557, 6] = -100\n# ---------- unit 7: Up from row 4 ----------\nW1[1:600:60, 7] = [0, 0, 6, 7, -30, -5.6, -4.8, -4, -3.2, 0]\nW1[7:600:60, 7] = [0, 0, 6, 7, -30, -5.